<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Swampy Lakes Shelter Loop</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:272-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.989467" lon="-121.568160"><ele>1769.6</ele><name>Swampy Lakes Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead th:swampy-lakes-sno-park (OSM relation 11960476); confidence: high; pdf_page: 273; book_elev_ft: 5700; quote: map 62: SWAMPY LAKES SNO-PARK 5700'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.003490" lon="-121.584270"><ele>1810.9</ele><name>West end of the Swampy Lakes flats (Swampy Tie junction)</name><desc>source: OSM: Swampy Lakes Trail #23 (way 279479053) meets Swampy Tie Trail #23.1 (way 878847315) at the SW edge of the Swampy Lakes wetland; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 274; quote: climbing a low divide then descending along the west end of the Swampy Lakes flats</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.004301" lon="-121.583655"><ele>1807.6</ele><name>Swampy Lakes Shelter</name><desc>source: OSM node 5716237824 Swampy Shelter; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 274; book_elev_ft: 5880; quote: The shelter sits on the north side of the wide meadow and 100 yards into the trees.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.003490" lon="-121.584270"><ele>1810.9</ele><name>West end of the flats (back from the shelter)</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 274; quote: From the shelter return to the meadow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.006550" lon="-121.579240"><ele>1793.8</ele><name>Turn south (Swampy Lakes Shelter Loop junction)</name><desc>source: OSM: east end of Swampy Tie Trail #23.1 where the Swampy Loop piste turns south (way 878964273); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 274; quote: ski east almost to the far end, where you turn south, continuing on the Swampy Lakes Shelter Loop Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.997500" lon="-121.576230"><ele>1821.6</ele><name>Loop meets Forest Road 4600-222</name><desc>source: OSM: Swampy Loop Trail #23.2 (way 878847319) meets Forest Road 4600-222 (way 5359369, piste Swampy Loop); confidence: high; pdf_page: 273; quote: map 62: 0.7 then 1.2 on the Swampy Lakes Shelter Loop back to the sno-park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.992080" lon="-121.567700"><ele>1774.5</ele><name>Forest Road 4600-222 at the Tangent Loop junction</name><desc>source: OSM: north end of path way 286208547 where Forest Road 4600-222 (way 5359369) meets the Tangent Loop (way 878847258), 0.15 mi above the sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 273; quote: map 62: the loop's east leg joins the trails just north of the sno-park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.989467" lon="-121.568160"><ele>1769.6</ele><name>Swampy Lakes Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high; pdf_page: 274; quote: Climb gently through pines, cross a divide, then descend to the trailhead.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Swampy Lakes Shelter Loop</name><desc>1. Swampy Lakes Sno-Park -&gt; West end of the Swampy Lakes flats (Swampy Tie junction): osm (high), 1.52 mi | 2. West end of the Swampy Lakes flats (Swampy Tie junction) -&gt; Swampy Lakes Shelter: straight (medium), 0.06 mi | 3. Swampy Lakes Shelter -&gt; West end of the flats (back from the shelter): straight (medium), 0.06 mi | 4. West end of the flats (back from the shelter) -&gt; Turn south (Swampy Lakes Shelter Loop junction): osm (medium), 0.34 mi | 5. Turn south (Swampy Lakes Shelter Loop junction) -&gt; Loop meets Forest Road 4600-222: osm (high), 0.66 mi | 6. Loop meets Forest Road 4600-222 -&gt; Forest Road 4600-222 at the Tangent Loop junction: osm (high), 0.68 mi | 7. Forest Road 4600-222 at the Tangent Loop junction -&gt; Swampy Lakes Sno-Park (finish): osm (medium), 0.23 mi</desc>
